# The Octane benchmark harness is a bash script, and the workflow's win-x64 leg
# runs it through Git Bash on a Windows runner. Git Bash cannot execute a script
# checked out with CRLF line endings — it fails on the stray `\r` in the shebang
# — so pin shell scripts to LF rather than depending on whatever `core.autocrlf`
# the runner image happens to set. Every .sh in the tree is already LF, so this
# records the invariant instead of changing anything.
*.sh text eol=lf
